  "comment": "Keyring authority rotation. Each case starts from an approved source whose authority came from an initial keyring (initialTrusted/initialRevoked, signed by the reviewed pin), then republishes the keyring. PIN, ROT and OLD stand for the fingerprints below; ARCH stands for an unrelated global signing key (an Arch/CachyOS or administrator key) outside the oniomarchy authority. A revocation may name only a primary this source already owned (previously accepted or revoked, or the pin): pacman-key --populate applies it to the shared keyring, so the archive's own trusted list grants no revocation authority and a signer it introduces is not revocable in the same archive. A case may name an accepted intermediate keyring (\"via\") applied before the final one.",
